text:
devin: heads-up — multiple customers reported a janky / frozen chart when switching tenant in the console. reproducing locally, chart frame drops for ~500-800ms and network shows a burst of telemetry fetches. :eyes:

maya: ugh. is this only on project switch or navigation in general? priority?

devin: only when you change tenant/project from the header. steps: 1) open heatmap 2) switch tenant 3) chart blocks until telemetry returns. noise + multiple chunk loads.

sanjay: can you paste the network entry? maybe we’re double-loading the heatmap chunk or rehydrating whole widget.

devin: paste: `GET /api/telemetry?scope=tenant&id=proj-123` x3 in <100ms, and `chunk-heatmap.js` fetched twice. also console: `Hydration mismatch: expected node with key chart-abc`

anna: that hydration mismatch likely from store reset on tenant change. our tenant middleware currently nukes session state and reinitializes stores (which resets chart keys). will investigate.

maya: timeline: perf-bot synthetic monitor spiked at 2026-03-19T12:14:03Z with 2.3s TTI on switch. might be correlated. @perf-bot any traces?

perf-bot: synthetic-alert: console/tenant-switch TTI spike > 2s at 2026-03-19T12:14:03Z. trace-id: 00-abc123-...-01. see /synth/traces/1912340123

kevin: quick win candidates: 1) debounce the telemetry fetch on tenant switch (250ms) to avoid duplicate fetches when header rapid-fires, 2) preserve chart component key across tenant change so it doesn't fully remount unless schema changes, 3) lazy-load heatmap chunk with prefetch so second load doesn't block main thread.

devin: I can prototype the debounce and key-preserve hotfix. simple: track pending switch timer in header, clearTimeout if another switch within 250ms.

anna: also check our Redux action: we dispatch RESET_ALL_STORES synchronously on tenant change. If we instead dispatch a soft-swap that patches only identity slices, we can avoid remounts. that’s less risky than re-architecting charts.

sanjay: looking at bundle analysis: heatmap chunk is 420kb gz, includes d3 + heavy utils. we can tree-shake some parts and move expensive math into a web worker. that would remove main-thread pressure.

kevin: proposed quick code (devin can include in PR):
```
// header.tsx
let switchTimer: number | null = null;
function onTenantSelect(id){
  if (switchTimer) clearTimeout(switchTimer);
  switchTimer = window.setTimeout(()=>{
    navigateToTenant(id);
  }, 250);
}
```
Preserve key: `<Chart key={chartStaticKey} />` instead of dynamic tenant-backed key.

maya: agree prioritize debounce + avoid reset. then follow up with chunk split + worker. plan: canary behind `tenant-switch-debounce` feature flag for 50% of hosts.

devin: ok creating PR for debounce + change to avoid RESET_ALL_STORES. will include e2e that asserts no `chunk-heatmap.js` double-fetch and no hydration warning. linking when ready. :+1:

perf-bot: deploybot: canary deploy queued for eng-platform with flag tenant-switch-debounce=true on 50% infra. deploy-id: canary-1912340200

anna: once PR merged, lets run synthetic again and watch TTI and frame drops. target: reduce median TTI on tenant-switch from 1.8s -> <700ms.

kevin: i'll take worker spike work after the canary, will open RFC for worker migration and chunk-splitting heuristics.

devin: thanks team — will post PR + quick repro screencast in thread. :zap:
